{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\fs24 Vice Chairman Herr reported on her tour of Recovery House of Central Florida and their upcoming gala, the Seminole County Public School's Annual Foundation Night of Impact, and her attendance at the legislative session. She mentioned she was asked why she doesn't attend Sanford's State of the City luncheon, and advised she is not a member of the Chamber and has never been invited, which turned into an invitation. She got to meet the new owners of the Sanford mall who talked about their vision for the property. HSN gave her the opportunity to present Kim Fogle with the Thomas C. Chapmon, Jr., Community Champion Award, and it was really nice to see a project in Seminole County get recognized. \par
\par
The Vice Chairman stated she has asked County staff to look at two parcels of land that may become available that are adjacent to the Smith Canal and may be valuable for drainage or future work. They are not on the market yet, but the owner has reached out and she's connected them to the team so they may be hearing more about that at some point.\par
\par
She gave a reminder to County staff about open enrollment.\par
