\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\fs24 Kim Ornberg, Environmental Services Director, addressed the Board and provided the department's budget presentation as included in the agenda backup. There were several questions from the Board. Commissioner Zembower discussed issues with tire reclamation and recycling. With the amount of property that the County owns, there is an opportunity for private-public partnerships to bring an entity in to not only handle the County's tire load, but also profit the ability to use that reclamation for the surrounding counties that otherwise are paying haulers to come in, pick them up, and haul them wherever. Since the County has the asset to do it, he'd like for staff to look into it to see if they could get someone to do it. Chairman Herr agreed that there are a lot of opportunities for private-public partnerships on that land that are worth exploring. Mr. Gray advised staff is working on a Solid Waste Master Plan that incorporates a lot of today's discussion, and that will be coming to the Board in the future.\par
