\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\fs24 Alan Harris, Director of Emergency Management, addressed the Board and provided the department's budget presentation as included in the agenda backup. There was discussion regarding the State of Florida determining they would no longer fund WebEOC, and Mr. Harris advised that will have to be a new item in the Emergency Management budget. Commissioner Zembower stated in regard to some of the services the County provides on behalf of the cities, he would like to know the actual cost and value of those services that the cities otherwise would have to undertake themselves. Mr. Gray responded they have that list together. His plan for the July 14 BCC meeting is to bring forward a strategy on property tax reform, and he'll ensure that the Commissioner's request is on that list as well. Chairman Herr added she would like the list to disclose whether or not the cities are funding the expense for the County to provide the service.\par
}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\fs24 Chief Matt Kinley, Fire Department, addressed the Board and provided the department's budget presentation as included in the agenda backup. Commissioner Zembower asked what further conversations are happening with Volusia County in light of the County servicing the whole southeastern corridor of their county out of Station 42. There is a financial agreement between the Counties, but he asked if they intend on having any discussions with them as a property share that they may want to help pay for the infrastructure verses building their own station in the Lake Harney area. Mr. Gray explained he has had communication with their county manager. They increased the contribution to the County because they were not paying much, and they do not have plans to put a fire station in the southeast part of their county. Staff is putting some numbers together, and they are planning to talk with Volusia County. He isn't sure yet whether that'll be to contribute to the station or to contribute to the overall cost of what they're paying now on an annual basis for the calls for services. Commissioner Zembower pointed out Volusia County should have more skin in the game because his concern is their plan for additional development in that corridor.\par
}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\fs24 Johnny Edwards, Utilities Director, addressed the Board and provided the department's budget presentation as included in the agenda backup. Commissioner Constantine advised Altamonte Springs is making biosolids into energy and are going to fuel their wastewater treatment plant, or at least a large portion of it, with that. He asked if staff is working with Altamonte Springs to see if the County could do that also. Mr. Edwards answered staff is looking at that. It is a more recent initiative from a pretty large consulting firm in conjunction with Altamonte Springs, but staff is excited to see the results. If it makes sense, they would love to partner with them. Mr. Gray added staff is making sure to be present and part of the program.\par
}

