{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\fs24 Commissioner Zembower reported on the State of Our Schools luncheon. The Commissioner stated although they discussed Jetta Point today, he isn't certain that management has full direction on what's happening with Jetta Point. He understands the agenda item was not for surplusing the property. They made a promise, more than once, that it was going to be surplus. He thinks it is unfair to leave today without a plan or some direction to staff on whether they're going to uphold the promise they made to the taxpayers on what's to happen with that property, do something different, or do some hybrid version thereof. Chairman Herr advised she thinks the promise that was made "a million years ago" to surplus a piece of land can be upheld in a lot of different ways; it doesn't have to be upheld by liquidating the property immediately. She would like for the team to take away what was heard today and interact with all of the other places that were involved in this because it's extremely complicated based on the location and the jurisdictions and the nature of the land, and then come back with some good solutions. Based on the lack of information they have, she doesn't know that they have to give a directive right now. \par
\par
\par
Commissioner Zembower asked how they are funding improvements at Rolling Hills because it was supposed to come from surplusing Jetta Point as well as transferring the easements. Mr. Gray answered it was brought to the Board a couple of months ago that they would be using the One Penny for the development of Rolling Hills; and if there's any other funding, he will let the Board know. Commissioner Dallari commented staff should be given some sort of direction. He would like to see staff put a plan together with all of the different options so that they can understand all of the pros and cons and provide staff full direction. Commissioner Zembower asked how much time staff needs to be prepared to bring that information back to the Board. Discussion ensued and it was determined Mr. Gray will report back to the Board at the next meeting how much time he needs because there may be more issues like entrance, drainage, and wildlife; and they need to understand all of that.\par
}

