\par
The Vice Chairman discussed the recent Medical Examiner meeting. She advised the agenda item that they had a question about (whether or not it was for informational purposes or voting purposes) was determined not to be voted on. However, they were asking whether or not there were any objections for it to go back to the individual boards. It's basically changing the language in the contract that's currently in place to reflect how they are actually operating. Several board meetings ago, they realized that they are not operating in accordance with the agreement. They need to decide if they want to change the agreement to reflect the way they're operating, or if they want to change the way they're operating to reflect the agreement. They decided they want to amend the contract to reflect the actual process that's in place. So that change will go to the Board, and all of the other boards, for consideration and ratification and then go back to the Medical Examiner board. Discussion ensued. Kristian Swenson, Assistant County Manager, addressed the Board to clarify and explain the need for the amendment to the contract. Commissioner Dallari requested to see the contract and be briefed by staff so they're all on the same page before it's in front of the Board. Vice Chairman Lockhart responded the contract will make its way through the County Attorney's Office, and then staff will be setting up those briefings.\par
\par
The Vice Chairman discussed an uptick in bear activity in her district. Few residents know about the bear-management areas in other parts of the county or that there are tools that they can utilize to help limit human-bear interactions or the bears getting into the trash because all of their efforts have really been in those bear-management areas. She would like to look at that the next time they have those conversations.\par
