\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\fs24 Mr. Gray and Mr. Slot addressed the Board and presented the item as outlined in the agenda backup. There were Board comments and questions. Commissioner Zembower suggested staff reach out to Frank Martz, City of Altamonte Springs, to discuss floating solar arrays because the Commissioner isn't sure that those would be a returnable, measurable cost benefit to the taxpayers. He did point out available County-owned acreage in his district that would be ideal for solar-array fields if there was a benefit to taxpayers. Regarding the Seminal Moments dashboard, he requested staff to provide data about unfunded mandates coming from Tallahassee so that everybody knows what those are; and in addition, be able to capture anything that is out pacing the cost of living on an annual basis. Vice Chairman Lockhart stated it would be very interesting if staff could bring forward a suggested plan that is incremental so they can see the "crawl, walk, run" of what makes sense; and then they could do things in a more meaningful, practical way. Chairman Herr made the following requests and statements: they need to be clearly delineating on the dashboard recurring savings verses one-time savings; there should be no floating solar arrays in retention ponds that would be visible to the public; the dashboard should have drill-downs; they need to rephrase when they're talking about the concept of surplusing their properties; and at some point they need to memorialize the ideas that dropped to the floor.\par
