The Vice Chairman inquired if there was an update on prior direction for the County Manager to work with legal counsel for collective bargaining to talk about where this Board could potentially come together to have discussions to prepare for collective bargaining. Mr. Gray responded following that meeting, they set up individual meetings with each of the Commissioners, and all of them have been briefed by Mr. Mandel, who described the process they would go through. Regarding Vice Chairman Lockhart's inquiry about having a closed session early on to talk about strategy, he would leave that up to the Board. The feedback he got individually from the Commissioners was to wait until January when the contract is open, when the union then will propose changes to their contract. They would then have a closed session and the Board would discuss strategy with the negotiating team on how to move forward. However, if the Board wants to do it before then, he would just have to coordinate with Mr. Mandel. There was brief discussion and the consensus was to meet sooner but after the contract opens.\par
